271
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:33,277
Performance reviews?

272
00:27:34,153 --> 00:27:35,696
I simply felt bad for you.

273
00:27:36,572 --> 00:27:38,407
I didn't do a single thing wrong

274
00:27:38,657 --> 00:27:40,659
but I let it go because
I felt bad about the situation.

275
00:27:41,952 --> 00:27:43,245
And this is how you behave?

276
00:27:48,083 --> 00:27:50,794
I am just as uncomfortable

277
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,005
as you are.

278
00:27:54,173 --> 00:27:55,924
You aren't the only one suffering.

279
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:57,426
So stop making a fuss.

280
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,846
I'm done treating you like a senior.

281
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:02,972
You brought this upon yourself

282
00:28:02,973 --> 00:28:04,266
and you'll bear the consequences.

283
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:06,935
Understood?

284
00:28:12,608 --> 00:28:13,609
Get back to work.

285
00:28:29,583 --> 00:28:32,544
This happened on my first morning off
as team leader.

286
00:28:34,504 --> 00:28:36,048
Both of you,
pull yourselves together.

287
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:37,924
Don't get caught up in this nonsense

288
00:28:37,925 --> 00:28:40,259
when you should be focusing
on your work.

289
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:41,470
You're not kids anymore.

290
00:28:42,679 --> 00:28:44,972
- Yes, sir.
- I'm sorry.

291
00:28:44,973 --> 00:28:46,016
I'm sorry.

292
00:29:06,203 --> 00:29:07,204
Come in.

293
00:29:14,127 --> 00:29:16,046
This is the sales record
for last week.

294
00:29:17,506 --> 00:29:19,341
And here's the report
on the new project.

295
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:22,760
At this rate, I'll be buried
under all this paperwork.

296
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:26,723
And I graphed the shifts
in consumer patterns year-over-year.

297
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:28,849
Here are the overseas brand sales

298
00:29:28,850 --> 00:29:31,728
categorized by region,
as you requested.

299
00:29:32,104 --> 00:29:33,689
Do you know what your problem is?

300
00:29:34,690 --> 00:29:36,941
I have so many.
I'm not sure which one.

301
00:29:36,942 --> 00:29:38,819
You don't give me
a moment to breathe.

302
00:29:39,236 --> 00:29:40,904
You need to pace my workload.

303
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:44,573
That, I didn't consider.

304
00:29:44,574 --> 00:29:46,702
The same goes
for how you treat your subordinates.

305
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:48,829
I heard Team 5 is a mess.

306
00:29:49,496 --> 00:29:50,579
Yes.

307
00:29:50,580 --> 00:29:52,039
Mr. Gong surprised me.

308
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,499
He's got quite a temper.

309
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:54,751
He learned that all from you.

310
00:29:55,335 --> 00:29:56,712
And I learned it from you, Ms. Park.

311
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:59,881
How's Laknes looking?
Do you think it'll go well?

312
00:30:00,299 --> 00:30:01,924
You know Mr. Gong.

313
00:30:01,925 --> 00:30:03,259
He always delivers
above expectations.

314
00:30:03,260 --> 00:30:04,970
He's got a good grasp
of the big picture too.

315
00:30:06,888 --> 00:30:10,017
Big-picture thinking is
what causes the biggest disasters.

316
00:30:10,392 --> 00:30:12,476
- Keep an eye on him.
- Yes, ma'am.

317
00:30:12,477 --> 00:30:14,603
And help him smooth things over
with Mr. Yang.

318
00:30:14,604 --> 00:30:16,481
What is bound to happen will happen.

319
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:18,817
But you can't leave a mess
sitting there.

320
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:20,944
Understood, ma'am.

321
00:30:21,236 --> 00:30:22,237
If you'll excuse me.

322
00:30:28,869 --> 00:30:32,622
I told you pacing is key, Mr. Jang.

323
00:30:43,967 --> 00:30:46,011
- Ju-hui.
- Yes, Ms. Joo?

324
00:30:46,261 --> 00:30:47,386
Are you looking for something?

325
00:30:47,387 --> 00:30:49,306
I'm looking for last year's catalog.

326
00:30:49,556 --> 00:30:50,973
For what?

327
00:30:50,974 --> 00:30:54,352
Osiris's design for this year
seems familiar.

328
00:30:54,353 --> 00:30:55,812
I want to dig around and check.

329
00:30:58,982 --> 00:31:01,485
Let me ask you something.

330
00:31:02,152 --> 00:31:05,530
Is your team taking over any brands
from another team?

331
00:31:06,615 --> 00:31:07,783
Like what?

332
00:31:08,033 --> 00:31:09,242
I'm just wondering

333
00:31:09,826 --> 00:31:13,830
if you are supposed to get anything
from Team 4 or 5.

334
00:31:17,292 --> 00:31:19,920
I'm not sure about such details.

335
00:31:21,630 --> 00:31:22,672
You aren't?

336
00:31:22,964 --> 00:31:24,924
Do you want me to look into it?

337
00:31:24,925 --> 00:31:26,551
No, it's fine.

338
00:31:27,677 --> 00:31:31,598
Let me know
if you hear anything, okay?

339
00:31:32,474 --> 00:31:33,475
Sure, Ms. Joo.

340
00:31:34,810 --> 00:31:36,478
- Keep up the good work.
- Thanks.

341
00:32:03,505 --> 00:32:05,132
Hello, Mr. Jang.

342
00:32:07,342 --> 00:32:08,343
I'm sorry?

343
00:32:15,809 --> 00:32:16,852
I knew it.

344
00:32:17,352 --> 00:32:19,020
I knew I'd find you here.

345
00:32:22,524 --> 00:32:24,692
Everyone probably knows I'm up here.

346
00:32:24,693 --> 00:32:26,486
That's why nobody else is coming up.

347
00:32:26,987 --> 00:32:28,320
I'm allowed up here, right?

348
00:32:28,321 --> 00:32:30,282
After all, I was your first mentor.

349
00:32:31,450 --> 00:32:33,660
I really started off
on the wrong foot.

350
00:32:35,871 --> 00:32:38,247
Man, the guy who got smacked
is working hard

351
00:32:38,248 --> 00:32:40,625
but the guy who threw the punch
is in distress.

352
00:32:41,251 --> 00:32:42,669
Where did that even come from?

353
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:46,256
It was bound to happen
sooner or later.

354
00:32:46,506 --> 00:32:48,842
Once? You should've done it
dozens of times already.

355
00:32:51,386 --> 00:32:52,887
So should I pat myself on the back?

356
00:32:52,888 --> 00:32:53,889
No.

357
00:32:54,431 --> 00:32:57,391
You should've either done it
dozens of times

358
00:32:57,392 --> 00:32:58,894
or kept swallowing it until the end.

359
00:33:00,687 --> 00:33:03,148
It must be driving you nuts
to go back down there and face him.

360
00:33:04,608 --> 00:33:05,609
Mr. Jeong.

361
00:33:06,318 --> 00:33:07,903
Remember back when we were
on Mr. Jang's team?

362
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:10,571
I used to get chewed out
all the time.

363
00:33:10,572 --> 00:33:11,615
I know.

364
00:33:11,990 --> 00:33:13,408
I'm only saying this now

365
00:33:13,867 --> 00:33:16,035
but we used to bet
on when you'd quit.

366
00:33:16,036 --> 00:33:17,954
The most ridiculous thing
back then was...

367
00:33:18,955 --> 00:33:20,039
Wait, you placed bets?

368
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:21,123
Yes.

369
00:33:21,124 --> 00:33:22,209
Go on. Tell me.

370
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:25,670
Anyway, the most ridiculous thing was

371
00:33:26,129 --> 00:33:28,631
when Mr. Jang completely
tore me apart

372
00:33:28,632 --> 00:33:31,592
and then acted all friendly,
throwing an arm around my shoulder.

373
00:33:31,593 --> 00:33:33,552
Tell me about it.
I fell for that many times.

374
00:33:33,553 --> 00:33:36,722
So I was 100 percent convinced
he was a psycho, a sociopath

375
00:33:36,723 --> 00:33:38,432
or whatever kind of path out there.

376
00:33:38,433 --> 00:33:40,726
I still think so.
That guy's a walking mental case.

377
00:33:40,727 --> 00:33:43,813
But now that I'm in those shoes

378
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:47,150
I wonder if I should go down there

379
00:33:48,151 --> 00:33:49,569
and act all friendly with him.

380
00:33:50,529 --> 00:33:53,448
Whenever Mr. Jang pulled that stunt

381
00:33:53,823 --> 00:33:56,283
I took it as a sign to sweep it
under the rug and move on.

382
00:33:56,284 --> 00:33:57,493
Why?

383
00:33:57,494 --> 00:33:59,078
Because corporate life is what it is.

384
00:33:59,079 --> 00:34:00,539
You just sweep it under the rug.

385
00:34:01,540 --> 00:34:03,083
Yang Jun-ho will probably
do the same.

386
00:34:03,667 --> 00:34:06,169
Should I do the same as Mr. Jang?

387
00:34:06,795 --> 00:34:09,046
Then you'll turn
into a psychopath as well.

388
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:10,382
- Oh, jeez!
- Oh, my gosh!

389
00:34:10,882 --> 00:34:11,883
Oh, man.

390
00:34:12,592 --> 00:34:14,593
How long have you been standing here?

391
00:34:14,594 --> 00:34:18,014
Look at you punks,
badmouthing your boss at work.

392
00:34:19,933 --> 00:34:21,601
You, follow me.
We're going somewhere.

393
00:34:23,645 --> 00:34:24,812
As for you, we'll talk tomorrow.

394
00:34:24,813 --> 00:34:26,356
Sir, that's not what I meant.

395
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:28,525
Hey, cover for me.

396
00:34:29,526 --> 00:34:31,570
You called him a psychopath first.

397
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:57,971
If you put half as much heart into me
as you do beef

398
00:34:58,305 --> 00:34:59,723
I'd carry you on my back.

399
00:35:02,267 --> 00:35:03,977
This is your treat today.

400
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,938
It's the unwritten rule to buy beef

401
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:09,440
if you get caught
badmouthing your boss.

402
00:35:09,441 --> 00:35:11,401
I was planning
on treating you, anyway.

403
00:35:12,193 --> 00:35:13,194
Look at this punk.

404
00:35:13,570 --> 00:35:16,238
No excuses, no denial...

405
00:35:16,239 --> 00:35:17,781
How shameless of you.

406
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:19,075
Thank you.

407
00:35:22,037 --> 00:35:23,121
Anyway...

408
00:35:23,913 --> 00:35:26,791
Are you sorting out the brands
to hand over to Team 1?

409
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:29,002
Wait.

410
00:35:29,544 --> 00:35:31,171
Is that officially locked in
for Team 1?

411
00:35:31,421 --> 00:35:33,340
Why bother asking?
You know how this works.

412
00:35:34,299 --> 00:35:35,925
Let's get Kim his promotion.

413
00:35:37,552 --> 00:35:40,095
I'll sort everything out
and hand it over by this week.

414
00:35:40,096 --> 00:35:41,430
What's there to think about?

415
00:35:41,431 --> 00:35:43,350
Just dump over
all the borderline ones.

416
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:45,727
They might look borderline to others

417
00:35:47,062 --> 00:35:49,104
but they're like my own kids.

418
00:35:49,105 --> 00:35:50,814
That's why I gave you Laknes.

419
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:53,818
A kid who'd get into SNU
without going to cram school.

420
00:35:55,028 --> 00:35:56,613
You punk.

421
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:04,788
This may be overstepping

422
00:36:05,455 --> 00:36:08,875
but is Mr. Jeong completely
written off for promotion?

423
00:36:11,378 --> 00:36:12,795
He's the one refusing to do it.

424
00:36:12,796 --> 00:36:14,214
It's not like I'm blocking him.

425
00:36:27,018 --> 00:36:28,561
Hey, over here.

426
00:36:29,979 --> 00:36:30,980
I told him to come.

427
00:36:31,815 --> 00:36:33,273
It's not like you're sworn enemies.

428
00:36:33,274 --> 00:36:34,609
He can be here.

429
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:37,862
But...

430
00:36:38,697 --> 00:36:39,822
Are you leaving?

431
00:36:39,823 --> 00:36:41,865
I'll take care of the bill.

432
00:36:41,866 --> 00:36:43,034
You guys finish up.

433
00:36:43,660 --> 00:36:44,661
Oh, right.

434
00:36:45,036 --> 00:36:46,287
When I acted friendly with Mr. Jeong

435
00:36:46,663 --> 00:36:50,125
I didn't mean to sweep
all the grudges under the rug.

436
00:36:50,709 --> 00:36:52,293
I meant to clear the air and move on.

437
00:36:54,546 --> 00:36:56,715
What are you waiting for?
Go sit down.

438
00:36:57,549 --> 00:36:58,550
I'm sorry?

439
00:37:14,023 --> 00:37:16,609
I was really craving beef today.

440
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:21,030
But I ended up
having it with you, Mr. Yang.

441
00:37:22,407 --> 00:37:24,617
Why the sudden switch back
to formality?

442
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:27,662
Obviously, I'll keep
speaking formally to you.

443
00:37:30,290 --> 00:37:32,041
Why are we pushing things this far?

444
00:37:35,462 --> 00:37:37,546
I think we need a drink for this.

445
00:37:37,547 --> 00:37:38,548
Yes, absolutely.

446
00:37:45,638 --> 00:37:46,639
Mr. Yang.

447
00:37:47,807 --> 00:37:49,225
Can I ask you something?

448
00:37:50,226 --> 00:37:51,478
Go ahead and shoot.

449
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:57,192
Am I such an important person
in your life?

450
00:38:00,528 --> 00:38:03,198
I'm not sure what you mean by that.

451
00:38:04,491 --> 00:38:05,575
You see

452
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:09,329
a major personal event
happened to me last weekend.

453
00:38:10,205 --> 00:38:11,706
It was life-changing enough...

454
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:16,503
to make me reflect on my whole life.

455
00:38:18,630 --> 00:38:20,381
But thinking about it all weekend...

456
00:38:22,425 --> 00:38:25,303
I realized my biggest obstacle
in life right now...

457
00:38:28,264 --> 00:38:29,474
is none other than you.

458
00:38:34,521 --> 00:38:35,647
So I asked myself

459
00:38:36,105 --> 00:38:39,441
if you were really
that important a person to me.

460
00:38:39,442 --> 00:38:40,527
The answer was no.

461
00:38:41,486 --> 00:38:43,362
I'm sure it's the same for you.

462
00:38:43,363 --> 00:38:44,780
We're just two individuals

463
00:38:44,781 --> 00:38:47,826
who lived different lives
for 30 years before crossing paths.

464
00:38:48,618 --> 00:38:50,537
If we click, that's great.

465
00:38:51,287 --> 00:38:54,249
But if we don't, there's no need
to stress or panic over it.

466
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:57,459
- Well, I suppose so.
- Right.

467
00:38:57,460 --> 00:38:59,754
We're not that important
to each other.

468
00:39:01,673 --> 00:39:03,258
There's no point
in fighting like this.

469
00:39:06,427 --> 00:39:08,388
Let me ask you straight up.

470
00:39:11,307 --> 00:39:12,642
Up until now

471
00:39:13,935 --> 00:39:15,353
what was your actual deal with me?

472
00:39:20,942 --> 00:39:22,735
- Let's drink another glass.
- Sure.

473
00:39:38,459 --> 00:39:41,588
Do you honestly see yourself
as the victim here?

474
00:39:45,049 --> 00:39:48,260
What do you take
your team members for?

475
00:39:48,261 --> 00:39:49,262
I mean...

476
00:39:49,596 --> 00:39:52,765
Have you ever once consulted us

477
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:55,768
before making critical decisions?

478
00:39:57,270 --> 00:40:02,149
I've never once felt like
a valued member of this team

479
00:40:02,150 --> 00:40:05,695
working alongside you
during my time here.

480
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:08,948
Think about it.

481
00:40:09,616 --> 00:40:12,619
I didn't start out
treating you awfully.

482
00:40:18,291 --> 00:40:21,210
When I started working under you,
I promised myself.

483
00:40:21,628 --> 00:40:23,588
I'd stop expecting respect
just because I'm your senior.

484
00:40:23,838 --> 00:40:25,965
I'd just focus on doing my best
as a team member.

485
00:40:27,175 --> 00:40:28,676
But you?

486
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:32,639
You have no respect for your team,
let alone senior respect.

487
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:36,350
You never care
about what's going on in our heads

488
00:40:36,351 --> 00:40:38,226
or what struggles we face on the job.

489
00:40:38,227 --> 00:40:40,063
You never show an ounce of curiosity.

490
00:40:40,313 --> 00:40:44,150
All you care about is whether
something meets your standards.

491
00:40:45,193 --> 00:40:46,486
This is a workplace.

492
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:48,904
We're here to get a job done.

493
00:40:48,905 --> 00:40:49,906
Right.

494
00:40:50,281 --> 00:40:51,824
That's your perspective.

495
00:40:54,869 --> 00:40:56,579
You may not feel the same way

496
00:40:57,288 --> 00:41:00,083
but to me,
you are an important person.

497
00:41:06,255 --> 00:41:07,798
As you know

498
00:41:07,799 --> 00:41:10,009
my batch didn't enter
through open recruitment.

499
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:12,929
So our seniority
wasn't properly credited.

500
00:41:14,806 --> 00:41:16,264
But do you really think

501
00:41:16,265 --> 00:41:18,810
that's the only reason
you got promoted ahead of me?

502
00:41:19,936 --> 00:41:21,562
Are you saying there's more to it?

503
00:41:22,105 --> 00:41:23,106
Of course.

504
00:41:23,690 --> 00:41:25,733
You're simply better than me.

505
00:41:27,360 --> 00:41:29,320
Seniority aside

506
00:41:29,696 --> 00:41:32,990
I would've been promoted first
if I'd been more capable.

507
00:41:32,991 --> 00:41:34,450
That's how corporate works.

508
00:41:38,037 --> 00:41:40,206
But part of me
wanted to mess with you.

509
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:44,377
You're younger than me,
but you seemed better than me.

510
00:41:47,588 --> 00:41:49,841
Now that I've said it out loud,
I sound like a total idiot.

511
00:41:55,930 --> 00:41:57,140
Don't say that.

512
00:41:58,808 --> 00:42:01,185
I thought I fully understood
your frustrations

513
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:03,271
but I clearly didn't.

514
00:42:03,771 --> 00:42:04,772
I'm sorry.

515
00:42:06,065 --> 00:42:07,567
Anyway, I'm sorry.

516
00:42:08,651 --> 00:42:11,529
At the end of the day,
this happened because I fell short.

517
00:42:12,447 --> 00:42:15,324
Not at all. Hearing your side,
I wasn't entirely blameless.

518
00:42:18,411 --> 00:42:20,538
I'll hand in my resignation tomorrow.

519
00:42:21,414 --> 00:42:24,708
I'll handle all the handovers
before I leave

520
00:42:24,709 --> 00:42:25,710
so don't worry.

521
00:42:26,294 --> 00:42:27,377
Oh, right.

522
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:28,670
When I acted friendly with Mr. Jeong

523
00:42:28,671 --> 00:42:31,716
I didn't mean to sweep
all the grudges under the rug.

524
00:42:32,008 --> 00:42:33,593
I meant to clear the air and move on.

525
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:39,932
Is that really necessary?

526
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:44,896
I don't have the stomach
to keep working here.

527
00:42:45,855 --> 00:42:48,149
I acted like a jerk
to my younger boss

528
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,943
and got chewed out for it.

529
00:42:52,111 --> 00:42:53,779
By that logic,
I'm a lousy team leader

530
00:42:53,780 --> 00:42:55,906
who couldn't manage
a single team member

531
00:42:55,907 --> 00:42:58,326
and publicly humiliated him.

532
00:43:01,454 --> 00:43:02,455
To be honest

533
00:43:03,498 --> 00:43:05,332
I was thinking of quitting too.

534
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:06,459
Truly.

535
00:43:08,252 --> 00:43:11,255
But if we both walk out now

536
00:43:12,840 --> 00:43:15,218
won't we just be quitting
because we lost to each other?

537
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:17,386
Let's not do that.

538
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:20,973
Mr. Yang.

539
00:43:22,308 --> 00:43:23,351
Well...

540
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:26,687
Putting aside our personal clashes

541
00:43:27,522 --> 00:43:29,899
how do you
evaluate me professionally?

542
00:43:33,486 --> 00:43:34,612
I had those moments.

543
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:38,032
Like, "I hate this guy's guts,
but he's good at his job."

544
00:43:39,242 --> 00:43:42,078
All the brands we brought in
were on the verge of tanking.

545
00:43:42,745 --> 00:43:44,038
I give you that.

546
00:43:44,997 --> 00:43:46,414
Your ability to see the big picture

547
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:47,959
and push projects through
was impressive.

548
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:50,795
I felt the same way.

549
00:43:51,879 --> 00:43:54,423
Even when I thought
we didn't click at all

550
00:43:55,133 --> 00:43:56,592
I couldn't deny your competence.

551
00:43:57,176 --> 00:43:59,011
I thought your years of experience
really showed.

552
00:43:59,762 --> 00:44:02,807
You've got an eye for details
that others overlook.

553
00:44:07,186 --> 00:44:08,187
You think so?

554
00:44:16,863 --> 00:44:18,364
Which brings me to my point.

555
00:44:20,408 --> 00:44:21,617
Let's team up.

556
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:24,245
Team up?

557
00:44:24,537 --> 00:44:25,538
Mr. Yang.

558
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:28,749
Do you want to shake things up
with me?

559
00:44:31,711 --> 00:44:33,880
You're making me feel uneasy.

560
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:39,218
I'm going to turn
this company around.

561
00:44:42,096 --> 00:44:47,018
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

562
00:45:00,156 --> 00:45:02,742
GANGNAM

563
00:45:03,993 --> 00:45:06,161
Yes, sir, so...

564
00:45:06,162 --> 00:45:09,247
Take this chance to register
as a rental property business

565
00:45:09,248 --> 00:45:11,959
and learn how to issue
electronic tax invoices.

566
00:45:12,418 --> 00:45:14,044
That's how people trip
into tax evasion

567
00:45:14,045 --> 00:45:15,671
while trying to save on taxes.

568
00:45:16,589 --> 00:45:18,506
Yes, right.

569
00:45:18,507 --> 00:45:19,884
Okay, goodbye.

570
00:45:21,385 --> 00:45:23,054
Goodness, I'm sorry.

571
00:45:23,387 --> 00:45:24,763
- The call went on a bit too long.
- No.

572
00:45:24,764 --> 00:45:26,681
- It's fine.
- So you're looking

573
00:45:26,682 --> 00:45:28,684
into both commercial spaces
and apartments?

574
00:45:29,435 --> 00:45:31,937
Nothing's set in stone yet

575
00:45:31,938 --> 00:45:34,941
but my priority is
stable monthly rental income.

576
00:45:35,608 --> 00:45:36,983
Do you have enough capital?

577
00:45:36,984 --> 00:45:38,027
Or will you need a loan?

578
00:45:38,819 --> 00:45:40,612
I've budgeted for some

579
00:45:40,613 --> 00:45:43,240
but I'd rather avoid loans
if possible.

580
00:45:43,241 --> 00:45:46,493
You must be quite well-off
for someone young.

581
00:45:46,494 --> 00:45:48,411
- Are you an office worker?
- Yes.

582
00:45:48,412 --> 00:45:50,288
Smart choice.

583
00:45:50,289 --> 00:45:54,334
In this day and age, relying solely
on a salary gets you nowhere.

584
00:45:54,335 --> 00:45:55,418
If you have spare cash

585
00:45:55,419 --> 00:45:57,880
you need a solid fallback,
like owning a building.

586
00:45:59,757 --> 00:46:03,261
If I may ask,
what is your annual salary?

587
00:46:03,886 --> 00:46:05,805
Around 70 million won.

588
00:46:06,305 --> 00:46:07,847
Does that matter?

589
00:46:07,848 --> 00:46:10,141
Of course, it matters.

590
00:46:10,142 --> 00:46:13,312
That means your personal market value
is over three billion won.

591
00:46:13,688 --> 00:46:15,772
To take in 70 million a year in rent

592
00:46:15,773 --> 00:46:18,400
after taxes and expenses

593
00:46:18,401 --> 00:46:20,486
your property needs to be worth
at least three billion.

594
00:46:20,987 --> 00:46:23,154
Making that much in salary means

595
00:46:23,155 --> 00:46:25,907
you're walking around
with a three-billion-won price tag.

596
00:46:25,908 --> 00:46:27,201
We've got a VIP here.

597
00:46:29,287 --> 00:46:30,288
You're right.

598
00:46:30,663 --> 00:46:31,998
Hearing it that way

599
00:46:33,207 --> 00:46:34,916
I'm worth three billion.

600
00:46:34,917 --> 00:46:36,836
A lot of people buy lottery tickets
these days, right?

601
00:46:37,962 --> 00:46:41,382
That's because they don't realize
their own worth.

602
00:46:42,258 --> 00:46:44,844
Now, let's see.

603
00:46:45,386 --> 00:46:47,929
Apartments around this neighborhood
are solid.

604
00:46:47,930 --> 00:46:49,556
Commercial buildings
come with too many...

605
00:46:49,557 --> 00:46:50,640
Sir.

606
00:46:50,641 --> 00:46:53,102
I'm sorry,
but I'll come back another time.

607
00:46:53,352 --> 00:46:54,436
I'm sorry?

608
00:46:54,437 --> 00:46:55,770
Like you said

609
00:46:55,771 --> 00:46:58,649
a 3-billion-won guy shouldn't get
pushed around by 1.3 billion.

610
00:46:59,442 --> 00:47:00,860
What's this 1.3 billion won?

611
00:49:34,054 --> 00:49:36,056
Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
